 ["flow 0c85a3 flow-identifiers: Word-based flow ID — 2026-10-09 (2026-10-09)" "I would like the word-based flow ID, but maybe Astra can make a tool, a [Clojure] tool, to do the conversion between the first 33 bits of the identifier we use for the harness and the word thing. It can get a regular expression back so that we can find which session from the list of transcript files we have, or maybe we have a list of the alpha-numerical ID somewhere in the database, or maybe we just make a registry in the database. In the database, we just write this [Clojure]. Let's define it as if we would define the data-oriented design, object data-oriented, kind of like how we design with ethos and stuff. We should have some kind of skill that explains how we want the [Clojure] developed, if we don't already, based on how we do ethos and Rust. The first presentation is an ethos anatomy, and then the [Clojure] code uses that as a guide to create its specification for its data and its types."]
 ["flow ebbe30 metaflow-naming: Topic flows: psyche::{topic}, the layer, then the word-based flow id (2026-10-09)" "I would like to get a fable on Flow and a fable on Ethos, and a fable on another topic, but let's just start there: a fable and an opus. Let's get the vision together. Even if some of it is raw, let's use the recent vision and the one that's been repeated a lot, which hasn't been overridden by newer decisions or statements.\n\nStart these two topic flows with the psyche::{topic}, either core, flow, or ethos, and then the layer: primary and secondary. There are three things. We can put the flow ID after that, although that might be a bit long, but let's try it. I would like the word-based flow ID, but maybe Astra can make a tool, a [Clojure] tool, to do the conversion between the first 33 bits of the identifier we use for the harness and the word thing. It can get a regular expression back so that we can find which session from the list of transcript files we have, or maybe we have a list of the alpha-numerical ID somewhere in the database, or maybe we just make a registry in the database."]
 ["flow 875960 flow: the flow id is the harness's session id hash, so a transcript is found from it (2026-10-11)" "We need the hash from the harness so we have to start the harness before we get the flow ID, I think. I don't know why this got turned around here unless we're not using the harness hash anymore. There are different parts of the session ID depending on the harness, which is supposedly random, and that's what we're using. I don't know why now the proposal is that we create a hash before. We've been using the session ID hash so that we can find a transcript easily from the flow ID. Is my idea stupid somehow or why do you think it's better to not do that?"]
